  "situation": "At Ramstein Air Base, the Board president is preparing formal findings about the cause of a C-130J mishap under a preponderance-of-evidence standard. During the final approach, the first pilot reduced engine power early, and the aircraft’s descent rate increased substantially before touchdown. The second pilot recognized the excessive descent late, and the first pilot’s subsequent power increase was insufficient to prevent a hard landing. Evidence included visual, sensory, and instrument cues available to the pilots, while the details of their visual scans were not fully established. The aircraft landed short of the painted landing-zone markings, and the available weather evidence did not establish a significant adverse wind shift.",
